{"id":"s5","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":5,"of":6,"title":"Word order","titleHe":"סֵדֶר הַמִּלִּים","goal":"Know the default order, and what moving a word does.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Modern Hebrew is subject–verb–object, like English. Literary and biblical Hebrew often puts the verb first, which is why an old sentence can read as inverted before you've parsed it."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"הַיֶּלֶד קָרָא אֶת הַסֵּפֶר.","en":"The boy read the book. — ordinary"},{"he":"קָרָא הַיֶּלֶד אֶת הַסֵּפֶר.","en":"Read the boy the book. — literary, same meaning"},{"he":"אֶת הַסֵּפֶר קָרָא הַיֶּלֶד.","en":"It was the book the boy read. — fronted for emphasis"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Because the verb ending already tells you the person, Hebrew can drop the subject pronoun entirely in the past and future. הָלַכְתִּי is a complete sentence."}],"vocab":[{"he":"דַּוְקָא","en":"specifically, of all things","translit":"davka"},{"he":"גַּם","en":"also","translit":"gam"},{"he":"אֲפִלּוּ","en":"even","translit":"afilu"},{"he":"בִּכְלָל","en":"at all, in general","translit":"bichlal"},{"he":"כָּךְ","en":"thus, so","translit":"kach"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["misses, longs for","specifically, of all things","actually","accepted, customary"],"correct":1,"prompt":"דַּוְקָא","translit":"davka"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["there is, there are","never","arranged, tidy","also"],"correct":3,"prompt":"גַּם","translit":"gam"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["month","happy","the man","even"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אֲפִלּוּ","translit":"afilu"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["at all, in general","his","strength","sea"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בִּכְלָל","translit":"bichlal"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["and he saw","city","thus, so","on me, about me"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כָּךְ","translit":"kach"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “thus, so”?","options":["כֹּה","טֶרֶם","מַיִם","כָּךְ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “even”?","options":["מְדַבֵּר","אֲפִלּוּ","אֲבָל","סוֹף"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “at all, in general”?","options":["בִּכְלָל","כִּי","לִי","דּוֹד"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"בִּכְלָל","translit":"bichlal","en":"at all, in general"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["כָּךְ","thus, so"],["אֲפִלּוּ","even"],["גַּם","also"],["דַּוְקָא","specifically, of all things"],["בִּכְלָל","at all, in general"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “also”?","options":["אַרְבָּעָה","שְׁלוֹשָׁה","עֲדַיִן לֹא","גַּם"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["גַּם","אֲפִלּוּ","דַּוְקָא","בִּכְלָל"],"correct":1,"say":"אֲפִלּוּ","he":true},{"type":"build","tokens":["אֶת","הַסֵּפֶר","קָרָא","הַיֶּלֶד"],"answer":["הַיֶּלֶד","קָרָא","אֶת","הַסֵּפֶר"],"en":"The boy read the book. — ordinary"},{"type":"build","tokens":["הַסֵּפֶר","אֶת","הַיֶּלֶד","קָרָא"],"answer":["אֶת","הַסֵּפֶר","קָרָא","הַיֶּלֶד"],"en":"It was the book the boy read. — fronted for emphasis"},{"type":"type","q":"Write “even” in Hebrew","answer":"אֲפִלּוּ","hint":"afilu"}]}